            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Urdu for birth, then the Urdu for a newborn."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: پرورش کرنا",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "پرورش کرنا — parvarish karnā — \"to raise a child; to bring up\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "نانی نے میری پرورش کی۔ nānī ne merī parvarish kī. My grandmother brought me up."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past, with نے (he or she …): اس نے بیٹی کی پرورش کی, us ne beṭī kī parvarish kī."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "پرورش کرنا (parvarish karnā) is built from پرورش, usually traced to Persian parvarish, \"nurture\", and کرنا, \"to do\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for describing what you lived and felt."
